  "prefLabel": "Frl 403.03 Continuing Education Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Frl 403.03 Continuing Education Requirements.\n\n(a) Every embalmer and funeral director shall complete 14 hours of CE credits every biennial licensing period that includes a minimum of 4 hours of didactic instruction. Retired licensees working fewer than 20 hours per week may request a waiver pursuant to Plc 211 of some or all CE requirements.\n\n(b) Each licensee shall use the on-line system, described in Plc 308.04(b), to track and report the completion of CE credit.\n\n(c) Proof of successful program or course completion shall be in the form of a certificate which shall contain at a minimum the following:\n\n(1) The name of the provider;\n\n(2) The completion date of the CE program;\n\n(3) The name of the participant;\n\n(4) The title of the program; and\n\n(5) The number of CE credits the program or course has been assigned.\n\n(d) A maximum of 6 CE credits earned in excess of the 14 hour minimum, shall be carried forward and applied to the next reporting period.\n\n(e) CE credits shall not be recognized for the same program attended or completed twice within the same biennial licensing period.\n\nSource. #2344, eff 4-15-83; ss by #2986, eff 3-18-85; ss by #4357, eff 1-20-88, EXPIRED: 1-20-94\n\nNew. #6516, eff 5-24-97, EXPIRED: 5-24-05\n\nNew. #9387, eff 2-12-09 (from Frl 403.02); ss by #12129, eff 3-10-17; ss by #14645, eff 9-7-26, EXPIRES: 9-7-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/frl100-900.html"
